{"kind":"delta","request":4893,"seq":4902,"t":265901,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Markdown link checker.\\n\\nScans Markdown files for internal links and verifies that the targets\\nexist. Standard library only; no third-party dependencies.\\n\\nSupported link forms\\n--------------------\\n- ``[text](path/to/file.md)``      relative file links\\n- ``[text](dir/file.md#anchor)``   links with an anchor (anchor checked\\n  against ATX-style headings when possible)\\n- ``[text](https://.../foo.md)``   absolute URLs are checked only for\\n  http/https when ``--check-remote`` is given; skipped by default\\n- Image links ``![alt](img.png)``  are checked as file targets\\n- Autolinks ``<file.md>``         are checked as file targets\\n\\nLinks whose target does not exist are reported as ``MISSING``; targets\\nthat exist but whose anchor cannot be found are reported as ``NOANCHOR``.\\n\\nUsage\\n-----\\n    python linkcheck.py [FILES ...] [OPTIONS]\\n\\nWith no FILES, the current directory is scanned recursively for\\n``*.md`` files (skipping ``.git``, ``node_modules``, ``vendor``).\\n\\nExamples\\n--------\\n    # Check all Markdown files in the current directory tree\\n    python linkcheck.py\\n\\n    # Check specific files\\n    python linkcheck.py README.md docs/guide.md\\n\\n    # Include remote http/https checks (slow, subject to network issues)\\n    python linkcheck.py --check-remote\\n\\n    # Treat missing targets as warnings instead of errors\\n    python linkcheck.py --allow-missing\\n\\nOptions\\n-------\\n    --check-remote    Also verify http/https links (HEAD request)\\n    --allow-missing   Report missing targets but exit 0\\n    --base-dir DIR    Resolve relative links against DIR (default: the\\n                      directory of each file)\\n    --verbose         One line per link checked, not just failures\\n\\nExit codes\\n----------\\n    0  all links OK (or only warnings, with --allow-missing)\\n    1  one or more missing targets / failed remote checks\\n    2  usage error (bad arguments, no files found)\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport sys\\n\\n\\ndef main(argv=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Entry point. Returns the process exit code.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    # TODO(step 2): argument parsing, file discovery, link extraction\\n    print(\\\"linkcheck: not implemented yet\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    return 2\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    sys.exit(main())\", \"path\": \"linkcheck.py\"}","id":"call_04885d8bcd3b4d5c9e51536b","index":0,"name":"write"}}
