t → report `docs/beta.md:N: missing.md`, exit 1.\n\nNote: heading_slug is unused in step 2 — no problem, it's requested as a helper.\n\nLet me write the code.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"...docstring stays...\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport urllib.parse\n\nSKIP_DIRS = {\".git\", \"node_modules\", \"vendor\"}\n\n# Inline link: [text](target) — matches image links ![alt](...) too.\nLINK_RE = re.compile(r\"\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(([^()\\s]+)(?:\\s+\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\")?\\)\")\n\nFENCE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\s*(```|~~~)\")\n\n\ndef find_md_files(paths):\n    \"\"\"Collect .md files from the given files/dirs (recursively).\"\"\"\n    if not paths:\n        paths = [\".\"]\n    files = []\n    for p in paths:\n        if os.path.isfile(p):\n            files.append(p)\n        elif os.path.isdir(p):\n            for root, dirs, names in os.walk(p):\n                dirs[:] = sorted(d for d in dirs if d not in SKIP_DIRS)\n                for n in sorted(names):\n                    if n.lower().endswith(\".md\"):\n                        files.append(os.path.join(root, n))\n        else:\n            print(f\"error: {p}: no such file or directory\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return None\n    return sorted(set(files))\n\n\ndef extract_links(text):\n    \"\"\"Yield (line_number, target) for inline links, skipping code fences.\"\"\"\n    in_fence = False\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):\n        if FENCE_RE.match(line):\n            in_fence = not in_fence\n            continue\n        if in_fence:\n            continue\n        for m in LINK_RE.finditer(line):\n            yield lineno, m.group(1)\n\n\ndef is_local(target):\n    return not re.match(r\"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\", target)\n```\n\nWait — `mailto:foo@bar` has a scheme. `#anchor` is not a scheme. `is_local`: if it starts with a scheme, skip (except… no, remote is skipped in step 2). So:\n\n```python\ndef is_local(target):\n    \"\"\"True if target is a relative path (p