{"items":[{"key":"seam-6/message-48","score":2,"sha256":"002321fc4a8c540553b1e416a46c7de6317852670fa6634af3679d8d0c210478"},{"key":"seam-6/message-45","score":2,"sha256":"e508b96f11302792c56c1665c3a729aac1f5b98a6e1ae586d06a00e67ff5a026"},{"key":"seam-6/message-29","score":2,"sha256":"ff5921bd93c64b857f76929831283b3d38243c361e7bdcc4529ab77f10584f32"}],"kind":"recalled","recall":"literal","seq":10396,"t":1848669,"text":"<system-reminder>\n## Relevant memory\n\nUse the following memories only when they are directly relevant to the current request. Verify file/function claims before relying on them.\n\n### a step that called tools (seam-6/message-48)\n\nupdate_record {\"field\": \"decision\", \"content\": \"linkcheck.py scope (user-set): local links only, no network; --check-remote is a reserved no-op flag for now. Output format is `file:line: target` (missing) and `file:line: target (NOANCHOR)` (bad anchor); exit 1 if anything broken, 0 with --allow-missing, 2 on usage errors.\"}\nupdate_record {\"field\": \"pointer\", \"content\": \"docs/ is served by a background `python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1` (loopback only) that must stay running for the rest of the session — user will use it later; do not stop it.\"}\nupdate_record {\"field\": \"followup\", \"content\": \"Unimplemented in linkcheck.py: --check-remote (urllib HEAD requests), GitHub-style duplicate-heading suffixes (-1, -2), autolinks <file.md> (removed from docstring as unsupported).\"}\nupdate_record {\"field\": \"constraint\", \"content\": \"Dev server must use port 5180 (5173 is taken in this environment).\"}\n\n### an answer (seam-6/message-45)\n\nAnchor checking is in. Changes in `linkcheck.py`:\n\n- **`collect_headings(text)`** — gathers GitHub-style slugs of ATX headings (`#`–`######` + space), skipping code fences and stripping closing `##` sequences\n- **`check_file`** — links with a fragment now resolve the target file and verify `heading_slug(fragment)` is among its headings; pure `#anchor` links check the file itself; URL-encoding (`%20`) is decoded; statuses are `ok` / `missing` / `noanchor`\n- **`main`** — broken links still print `file:line: target`; anchor failures print `file:line: target (NOANCHOR)`; exit 1 on any breakage (still 0 with `--allow-missing`)\n- Docstring updated to match (dropped the unimplemented autolinks bullet)\n\nVerified on `docs/`:\n- `python3 linkcheck.py` → `docs/beta.md:3: missing.md` + `docs/beta.md:11: beta.md#no-such-heading (NOANCHOR)`, exit 1\n- Valid anchors pass: `beta.md#useful-section`, `alpha.md#alpha` show `(ok)` under `--verbose`\n- Edge cases: fenced `# Not a heading` ignored, `## Two Words ##` → `two-words`\n\nRemote links remain skipped per scope. Next step candidate: `--check-remote` (HEAD requests via `urllib`) or duplicate-heading handling (`-1`, `-2` suffixes).\n\n### an answer (seam-6/message-29)\n\nStep 2 done. In `linkcheck.py`:\n\n- **`find_md_files(paths)`** — recursive `.md` discovery (skips `.git`, `node_modules`, `vendor`); None on bad path\n- **`extract_links(text)`** — yields `(line, target)` for inline/image links, skips fenced code blocks\n- **`check_file(path, base_dir)`** — per-line results; skips scheme URLs (remote deferred) and pure `#anchor` links\n- **`main(argv)`** — argparse with `files`, `--base-dir`, `--allow-missing`, `--verbose`; `--check-remote` accepted but warns it's reserved; broken links printed as `file:line: target`\n- **`heading_slug(text)`** — GitHub-style slug, defined just above the guard (verified: `Hello, World!` → `hello-world`)\n\n`docs/` has `index.md`, `alpha.md`, `beta.md` cross-linking, with `beta.md` linking to a nonexistent `missing.md`.\n\nVerified runs:\n- `python3 linkcheck.py` → `docs/beta.md:3: missing.md`, exit 1\n- `--allow-missing` → same output, exit 0\n- `--verbose docs` → `(ok)` lines plus the failure, exit 1\n- `docs/index.md` alone → exit 0; bad path → exit 2\n\nStep 3 candidates: anchor checking via `heading_slug`, or `--check-remote`.\n\n</system-reminder>","turn":7}
