ions exist, no reference links exist either, so it's fine.\n\nHmm, another subtlety: `m.group(2) if m.group(2) else m.group(1)` — for collapsed `[text][]`, group 2 = \"\" → use group 1. ✓ For shorthand, group 2 = None → group 1. ✓ For full form, group 2 = label. ✓\n\ncheck_file:\n\n```python\n    try:\n        with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            text = f.read()\n    except OSError as e:\n        print(f\"error: {path}: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return None\n\n    ref_defs = parse_ref_definitions(text)\n    base = base_dir or os.path.dirname(path)\n    results = []\n    for lineno, target in extract_links(text, ref_defs):\n```\n\nmain: add `--json` argument and JSON output.\n\n```python\n    parser.add_argument(\"--json\", action=\"store_true\",\n                        help=\"print broken links as a JSON list instead of lines\")\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```python\n    if args.json:\n        payload = [\n            {\"file\": path, \"line\": lineno, \"target\": target, \"status\": status}\n            for path, lineno, target, status in broken\n        ]\n        print(json.dumps(payload, indent=2))\n    else:\n        for path, lineno, target, status in broken:\n            suffix = \" (NOANCHOR)\" if status == \"noanchor\" else \"\"\n            print(f\"{path}:{lineno}: {target}{suffix}\")\n    return 1 if broken and not args.allow_missing else 0\n```\n\nAdd `import json` at the top.\n\nDocstring options:\n\n```\n    --check-remote    Also verify http/https links (HEAD request)\n    --allow-missing   Report missing targets but exit 0\n    --base-dir DIR    Resolve relative links against DIR (default:\n                      the directory of each file)\n    --json            Print broken links as a JSON list instead of lines\n    --verbose         One line per link checked, not just failures\n```\n\nAlso, maybe add a note to the docstring: reference definitions themselves are not reported; only the links that use them. I'll add a sentence in the